                                                "sense_id": "7e67b260-f1a7-336d-9c1f-c914bcb1f257",
                                                "text": "The following notations are in common use: H#58;f#92;simeqg (rel A) means that H is a homotopy rel A from f to g...."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2355f1ff-3671-4480-bd27-daa498a9539a",
                                                "sense_id": "7e67b260-f1a7-336d-9c1f-c914bcb1f257",
                                                "text": "Then in n#92;gen', there is a map h#58;Z#92;toZ' such that h#124;A#61;g and gf#92;simeqf'h rel A, so the diagram above is commutative up to homotopy rel A."
